# React Component CSS Modules Pattern

When creating or editing React components, follow this implementation pattern.

## Component Rules

- Keep component markup semantic.
- Keep business logic separate from styling logic.
- Avoid unnecessary wrapper divs.
- Do not introduce new dependencies unless they are already used in the project or clearly necessary.
- Use CSS Modules for all component-scoped styles.
- Use TypeScript props interfaces or types for public component props.
- **File/folder names: kebab-case.** Export names: PascalCase (`export function ExampleCard`).

## Preferred Component Template

```tsx
import styles from './example-card.module.css';

type ExampleCardProps = {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  imageUrl?: string;
};

export function ExampleCard({ title, description, imageUrl }: ExampleCardProps) {
  return (
    <article className={styles.card}>
      {imageUrl ? (
        <div className={styles.imageWrap}>
          <img className={styles.image} src={imageUrl} alt="" />
        </div>
      ) : null}

      <div className={styles.content}>
        <h3 className={styles.title}>{title}</h3>
        {description ? <p className={styles.description}>{description}</p> : null}
      </div>
    </article>
  );
}
```

## Preferred CSS Module Template

```css
.card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 12px;
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  border-radius: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.imageWrap {
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.image {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
}

.content {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
  min-width: 0;
}

.title {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: clamp(18px, 2.5vw, 24px);
  line-height: 1.25;
}

.description {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .card {
    gap: 16px;
  }
}
```

## Review Checklist

Before finalizing code, verify:

- The component works on mobile width first.
- No horizontal overflow is introduced.
- Class names are imported from the module file.
- Interactive elements have accessible focus states.
- Text content has sensible wrapping or truncation.
- Images do not distort unexpectedly.
- Files use kebab-case naming per [feature-file-naming.mdc](./coding/feature-file-naming.mdc).
